  "_placeProps": "Master switch. false places NO furniture or clutter at all - lights and switches are unaffected, since those are fixtures rather than fillers. The layout below is kept intact so turning this back to true restores every piece exactly where it was.",
  "placeProps": false,


  "_placement": "Each prop is positioned relative to a ROOM from floorplan.json, never in absolute world coordinates - so if a room moves, its contents move with it. 'placement' is one of: wall (backed against the named wall, facing into the room), floor (free-standing, positioned by fractional u/v across the room), ceiling (hung from the ceiling), counter (sitting on a worktop, so it is raised to counter height automatically).",

  "_along": "For wall placement, 'along' is a FRACTION of that wall's length measured from its low-coordinate end - the south end of a north-south wall, the west end of an east-west wall. 0.5 is centred. For floor placement, 'u' runs west-to-east and 'v' south-to-north across the room, both 0..1.",

  "_sizeFeet": "Real-world [width, depth, height] of the object when stood facing you. This drives two things: the stand-in box drawn before you supply a model, and the automatic scale correction applied to the model you do supply - its measured bounds are compared against this and scaled to match. Get this roughly right and badly-scaled assets fix themselves.",

  "_asset": "A semantic key, NOT a filename. The asset library matches it against whatever is in Assets/_Project/Props/Incoming by keyword, and records the result in asset_map.json. Correct a bad match by editing that file, not this one.",

